1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.215
The reason for examining the pupils in primary eye care is to see if there's any obvious visible

2
00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:14.431
evidence of disease, such as cataract or trauma, and to see if the pupil constricts to bright light.

3
00:00:14.431 --> 00:00:21.245
This tells us if the optic nerve or retina at the back of the eye are healthy.

4
00:00:21.245 --> 00:00:26.857
Start by explaining what you're going to do and check the patient is happy.

5
00:00:26.857 --> 00:00:32.269
Then look at the eyes to see if the pupils are black, round and

6
00:00:32.269 --> 00:00:37.680
equal, and if there are any other signs such as squint or droopy,

7
00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:38.033
eyelid.

8
00:00:38.033 --> 00:00:43.680
Then the lights in the room then check the direct pupil response with a bright light

9
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.524
by looking for a brisk and obvious constriction.

10
00:00:46.524 --> 00:00:50.080
If this is present then the optic nerve and retina

11
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.642
at the back of the eye are likely to be healthy.

12
00:00:53.642 --> 00:00:56.880
If the pupil fails to constrict then there is likely

13
00:00:56.880 --> 00:01:01.714
to be disease of the optic nerve such as glaucoma or the retina such

14
00:01:01.714 --> 00:01:03.440
as detachment or blockage of

15
00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:04.122
blood supply.

16
00:01:04.122 --> 00:01:09.920
It can be hard to see the black pupil against the dark brown iris and so you'll

17
00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.789
have to get in close.

18
00:01:11.789 --> 00:01:15.900
When healthy the pupil should constrict briskly and obviously to bright

19
00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:17.695
light in a dim room.

20
00:01:17.695 --> 00:01:22.720
Even in this eye with a grey white pupil due to cataract the pupil

21
00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:28.320
should still constrict despite the cataract as long as the optic nerve and retina at the

22
00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:31.104
the back of the eye are healthy.

23
00:01:31.104 --> 00:01:35.480
If the pupil only constricts a little and slowly then there

24
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.431
is likely to be disease at the back of the eye and the visual

25
00:01:39.431 --> 00:01:40.560
outcome from cataract surgery

26
00:01:40.560 --> 00:01:41.782
may be poor.

27
00:01:41.782 --> 00:01:47.080
When the pupil response is entirely absent, the chance of visual improvement after

28
00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:49.666
cataract surgery is very low.

29
00:01:49.666 --> 00:01:54.320
Remember, when examining the pupil, first look to confirm

30
00:01:54.320 --> 00:02:00.480
It is black, round and equal and then in the dim room reacts briskly

31
00:02:00.480 --> 00:02:03.120
and obviously to a bright light.
